# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
Cargo.lock.bak
audit.toml.lock
# Ignore .cargo contents (local config.toml, credentials, registry caches) but
# keep audit.toml tracked -- it carries the reviewed advisory exemptions and CI
# needs it. Note the pattern must be `.cargo/*`, not `.cargo/`: git does not
# descend into an excluded *directory*, so a `!.cargo/audit.toml` negation
# under `.cargo/` would never be consulted.
.cargo/*
!.cargo/audit.toml
rust-project.json
.rust-analyzer/

